    "created_at": "2015-12-17T15:23:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-17T15:23:36Z",
    "body": "I guess the idea is to see if there are any examples of `<i>` usage that people might mistakenly use `<u>` for. (Ship names seem plausible to me, but apparently the OP thinks this mistake is so inconceivable that it's just misleading to list it.)\n\nPerusing https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-i-element, and combined with @zcorpan's examples above, it seems like \" a technical term\", \"an idiomatic phrase from another language,\" or \"a transliteration\" might be good examples of things people are mistakenly using `<u>` for that they should be using `<i>` for.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
