    "body": "@Ritsyy \nthis is clearer english:\n\"The `<i>` element should be used for technical terms, taxonomic designation, transliteration, a thought, or for labelling ship names in western texts.\"\n\n@domenic \n\n> but apparently the OP thinks this mistake is so inconceivable that it's just misleading to list it.\n\nsounds a little misrepresentative of the intention with this issue:\n\n> for labeling ship names in Western texts, the i element should be used.\n\n\"ship names\" was the ONLY example listed--thus, my question:\n\n> is it just a poor example which is part of a larger set of more useful/relevant examples not mentioned in the spec?\n\nadditionally, this is an **issue**-tracking system, not a **bug/mistake**-tracking system:\n\n> File an issue about the selected text\n\n<img width=\"1058\" alt=\"screen shot 2015-12-17 at 17 28 02\" src=\"https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/83606/11875152/9ffd49ea-a4e3-11e5-9d8a-3e8941f7b428.png\">\n\n:)\n",
